From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: ggml-cuda: tiled 1D im2col

A tiled, coalesced fast path for 1D im2col (IH == KH == OH == 1). A block
stages a channel-by-time input tile through shared memory, then consecutive
threads write consecutive output columns for a run of output rows. The generic
kernel strides across channels and re-reads every input element KW times.
Speeds up the NanoCodec 1D convolutions that go through im2col.

Upstream: candidate (needs a benchmark).

